{"id":"jump-game-ii","title":"Jump Game II","difficulty":"Medium","pattern":"Greedy","tags":["Greedy","Array","BFS"],"companies":{"google":2,"apple":1,"amazon":2,"microsoft":1},"description":"Same movement rule as Jump Game: from index `i` you may jump forward up to `nums[i]` positions. It is guaranteed that the last index is reachable.\n\nReturn the **minimum** number of jumps needed to go from index `0` to the last index.","examples":[{"input":"nums = [2,3,1,1,4]","output":"2","explanation":"Index 0 -> 1 -> 4."},{"input":"nums = [2,3,0,1,4]","output":"2"},{"input":"nums = [0]","output":"0","explanation":"Already at the last index."}],"constraints":["1 <= nums.length <= 10^4","0 <= nums[i] <= 1000","The last index is always reachable."],"hints":["Think of it as BFS where level k is the set of indices reachable in exactly k jumps. Those indices form a contiguous window.","Keep the right edge of the current window `cur_end` and the farthest index any element in the window can reach. When i hits cur_end, take one jump and move the window to `farthest`.","Stop scanning at n-2: once the window covers the last index no further jump is needed."],"function":"jump","signature":"def jump(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:","arg_types":{"nums":"List[int]"},"return_type":"int","compare":"exact","tests":[{"input":{"nums":[2,3,1,1,4]},"output":2},{"input":{"nums":[2,3,0,1,4]},"output":2},{"input":{"nums":[0]},"output":0},{"input":{"nums":[1,1,1,1]},"output":3},{"input":{"nums":[1,2,3]},"output":2},{"input":{"nums":[2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,